+## 2. Band layout
+
+| Window | Driven by | What it is |
+|---|---|---|
+| 0x17800000–0x178010FF | 0x40c5deb4–0x40c5e934 | **Not storage.** Disjoint code region; see §8 |
+| **0x17820000–0x17820FFF** | 0x4028d24c–0x4029acfc | **SDIO**: SD host controller, standard set at +0x000, vendor/PHY at +0x100–0x250 |
+| **0x17828000–0x178281FF** | 0x4028ecd4, 0x4029b834, 0x402a2bf0, 0x402a2d14 | **UHS2_1 lower page**, most likely the F_SDH30 set of the UHS-II slot. Five registers used |
+| **0x17828200–0x178283FF** | 0x4029b154–0x402a39a8 | **UHS2_1 / F_SDH40**: SD-4.x standard set at +0x000 with the UHS-II block at +0x080, vendor at +0x100 |
+| 0x17840000–0x17842840 | 0x40c5ea9c–0x40c6023c | **Not storage.** Disjoint code region; see §8 |
+| 0x17880000 (+0xc110) | 0x40c717ec–0x40c7187c | **Not storage.** USB 3 host; see §8 |
+
+No code in this image references 0x17830000.
+
+Within each file, "offset" below is relative to the window base in bold
+above. **Every access in the whole band is a 32-bit `LDR W` / `STR W`.**
+There is no byte or halfword access anywhere; 16-bit and 8-bit register
+fields are reached by read-modify-write of the containing word (e.g.
+0x4028EE1C–0x4028EE34 preserves bits 16–31 while setting bit 0 of Clock
+Control). The model therefore only has to answer word accesses.
