+## 4. UHS2_1 lower page — 0x17828000
+
+Five registers, all used only by the UHS-II bring-up and teardown. Only
+0xFC sits at an SD-standard offset, so **I cannot prove what this page is.**
+Two readings are consistent with the evidence:
+
+* It is the **F_SDH30 standard register set** of the UHS-II slot — supported
+  by the interrupt-name table (§1.1), by 0xFC decoding exactly like the
+  SDIO file's 0xFC, and by the fact that the SDIO instance also puts its
+  vendor area immediately above its standard set. Offsets 0x60, 0x78, 0x7C
+  and 0x94 would then be Socionext additions in the standard's reserved
+  space.
+* It is a **UHS-II PHY / link-sequencer page** and 0xFC is its own revision
+  register, which the firmware happens to gate on in the same idiom.
+
+The firmware does not distinguish them. What it does with each register is
+unambiguous:
+
+| Off | Width | Dir | What the driver does | Firmware address |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 0x60 | 32 | R | Polled for **bit 1 == 0** before continuing, 250 ms budget. Appears twice: at the end of UHS-II teardown, and after the SD clock is stopped | 0x4028EFA8 / 0x4028EFAC (`TBZ W8,#1`), 0x402A2CC4 / 0x402A2CC8 |
+| 0x78 | 32 | W | Written 1 immediately before internal-clock enable (0x4028EE18) and 0 during teardown (0x4028EFD4). A single enable bit | 0x4028EDF4 (base), 0x4028EE18, 0x4028EFD4 |
+| 0x7C | 32 | R | Polled for **bit 0 == 1** as the last step of teardown, after both clocks are off, 250 ms budget | 0x4028F040 / 0x4028F044 (`TBNZ W8,#0`) |
+| 0x94 | 32 | W, RMW | Link/PHY configuration plus a strobe in bit 0. 0x4028ECD4 writes 0, then 0x4050, then sets bit 0 (→0x4051). 0x402A2D14 writes 0x4441 or 0x4041 depending on vendor register 0x104 of the F_SDH40 file, then clears bit 0 | 0x4028EF64–0x4028EF74, 0x402A2D30 |
+| 0xFC | 32 | R | {Slot Interrupt Status[15:0], Host Controller Version[31:16]}, compared `>= 0x10000` as the gate for ADMA2. See §7 | 0x4029B8BC (build), 0x4029B8CC (load), 0x4029B8D0 (compare) |
+
